---- Changes since 1.0 ----
Added a page for setting up scheduled backups of some or all worlds on the server.
Added a warning message on the main page if the server version is out of date.
German translations from Raymond Vetter.
Added a list of recent events for a player to the Manage Player page.
---- Changes since 1.1 ----
Added a button to grant XP orbs / levels to a player.
Created the Daily Play Time page for displaying usage by user, and the ability to ban users who exceed daily limits.
---- Changes since 1.4 ----
Added support for the new log file format found in Minecraft 1.7.2.
---- Changes since 1.9 ----
World downloads and backups store symbolic links inside a world as links. If the world folder itself is a symbolic link, the operation fails and any existing backup is preserved.
Reusing a backup ZIP keeps files deleted from the world. If a path changed between a file or link and a directory, keeping both versions would prevent a restore. The backup then fails and preserves the existing ZIP. Choose a new destination to back up the current world.
World backups require room for the new ZIP in Webmin's temporary directory. When reusing a destination, the existing backup must be a regular file.
Backups made by earlier versions may contain copies of files that links inside a world pointed to. Make and verify a fresh backup before removing those older ZIPs.
